{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_rwxnc526orajt6wi25oslkg4bvgyqigzu6tmtx3qfpdrbdz3wb7q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases passed.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single tiny module: `void driver(float x)` prints the 4 native-endian object-representation bytes of `x` as `%02x` followed by `\\n`, via the `static` helper `print_hex`. `nm -D` on the C `.so` exports exactly one non-glue symbol: `driver`.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped (artifacts in crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | Raw `nm -D` for both `.so`s. C exports `{driver}`; Rust exports `{driver}`. **0 missing.** Audited both C files — nothing untranslated, nothing stubbed. `print_hex` is `static` in C and correspondingly private in Rust (required parity, not a gap). |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 19 rows. The mechanical grep for `RETURN_ERROR`/`return -1`/`NULL`/`assert`/`errno`/range checks returned **zero matches** — the API returns `void` and can't report failure. Rows therefore cover the real rejection surface: the dead `len<=0` loop guard, every IEEE-754 special encoding (sNaN payloads, ±0, subnormals, one-step-past-range), high-bit bytes, and the `stdout` failures the C *deliberately ignores* (ENOSPC via `/dev/full`, EBADF via a read-only fd 1, pre-poisoned `ferror`). E17/E18 document why \"out-of-range enum\" and \"null pointer\" are non-applicable **by construction** — verified structurally, not assumed. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 23 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: the `%02x` byte domain (exhaustive, all 4 positions), the full 32-bit input space, all 7 IEEE classes, all three `stdout` buffering modes, file/pipe/`/dev/null` targets, 0/1/many calls, buffer-boundary straddling, and interleaving with the caller's own `printf`. |\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n\n- **Feature space:** `Cargo.toml` had no `[features]`, and `CMakeLists.txt`/`driver.c` have no `option()`/`#ifdef`. So exactly **one** valid combination (empty set); `check_features.sh` derives the power set mechanically. `cargo check` clean for it and for the default set.\n- **43 differential cases**, all driving both libraries through `dlopen`+`dlsym` only (never calling Rust directly), ~90 000 randomized `driver` invocations per run from a fixed SplitMix64 seed. **43/43 pass** in all **4 build configurations** (empty/default features × dev/release).\n- **Symbol parity:** 0 missing exports, 0 unresolved non-libc imports (`ldd -r` clean).\n\n## Two harness bugs I had to fix (not translation bugs)\n\n1. libtest's parallel threads and its own progress output both use fd 1, which the captures redirect — that corrupted results and even propagated the `/dev/full` `ENOSPC` into the harness. Switched the target to `harness = false` with a strictly sequential runner that resets fd 1 after every case.\n2. `cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target, so the suite could have silently validated a stale `.so`. Added an mtime staleness guard that refuses to run (verified it fires).\n\n## Negative control\n\nBecause everything passed on the first attempt, I proved the suite isn't blind: `mutation_check.sh` breaks the Rust 8 ways (`%2x`, `%02X`, `to_be_bytes`, `len=3`, no newline, signed-char promotion, sNaN quieting, `-0.0` folding). **Every mutant was caught** (10–41 cases each), and `src/lib.rs` is restored — md5 unchanged.\n\nThe existing translation required **no correctness fixes**; only `Cargo.toml` (dev-deps + test target) and new test/script/doc files were added, and `c_src/` sources are untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":504,"cache_read_input_tokens":130281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":504,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9bbe3f16-c6d5-4cad-92b7-8046b91b3c20","uuid":"46a7a298-f9ba-4171-a73a-021d2edeb832","timestamp":"2026-08-18T10:05:45.654Z"}
